NAME: a pointer's value keeps an if's jump
DESCRIPTION: p (6) points from its cell across the if's jump to target: fusing the if would move target and not p, so the jump stays (d-7d2612-6222c1); see behtests/fusion_pointer_span.beh
SRC:
(program
  (start top)
  (let (p 6)
    (seq (DAT 0 (store p)) (label top) (if (EQ 1 1) (NOP)) (MOV 9 (Ind p)) (JMP 0)
      (label target) (DAT 7 7))))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b
ORG top

_LET1 
  DAT    #0     , #6     
top   
  SEQ.AB #1     , #1     
  JMP    $_IF8  , #0     
  NOP    #0     , #0     
_IF8  
  MOV.AB #9     , @_LET1 
  JMP    #0     , #0     
target
  DAT    #7     , #7     
  DAT    $0     , $0     